uction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:6fa8f1a645a3a6baef997fef080980cfb131d9b5ebedb85ceb3fcf7075bc5ca1","file":"preprints/Compatibility-entropy-and-the-spectrum-of-a-Thorp-sweep-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex","line":24,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"76c3b7acf9c91ac7281d0cba093c776156ddfd07927bb623839cce1cc5029d62","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Compatibility-entropy-and-the-spectrum-of-a-Thorp-sweep-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:6fa8f1a645a3a6baef997fef080980cfb131d9b5ebedb85ceb3fcf7075bc5ca1","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Compatibility-entropy-and-the-spectrum-of-a-Thorp-sweep-September-26-2026/build/sections/00-introduction.tex#L24"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{tra:duality:weighted}\\label{tra:duality:weighted-statement}\nThere are absolute constants $L,C_0>0$ such that the following holds. Put $m=\\sqrt n$, assume $m/2\\le A,D\\le2m$, and take $m$ sufficiently large that $\\theta=1-L/\\log m>0$. For all nonnegative functions $w_i:S_D\\to[0,\\infty)$ and $v_k:S_A\\to[0,\\infty)$,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{tra:duality:eq5}\n \\frac{n!}{|R||C|}\\,\n \\mathbb E_U\\!\\left[\\mathbf1_{\\mathcal I}\n       \\prod_{i=1}^A w_i(r_i)\\prod_{k=1}^D v_k(c_k)\\right]\n \\le e^{C_0n^{.54}}\n       \\prod_{i=1}^A(\\mathbb E w_i^{1/\\theta})^\\theta\n       \\prod_{k=1}^D(\\mathbb E v_k^{1/\\theta})^\\theta .\n\\end{equation}\nThe expectations on the right are uniform on the indicated symmetric groups, and logarithms are natural."}
